  "style": {
    "id": "marionette",
    "name": "Marionette",
    "description": "A lacquered, brightly painted wooden string puppet on a small toy-theatre stage (pale painted-sky backdrop, red pleated curtains, plank floor), worked from above by a wooden control bar with a rocking leg bar and a rail of painted name tags. A closed-form string rig is the whole mechanism: the bar's pose (lift, pitch, roll, yaw, leg-bar rock) and the pull on each tagged string are the only animated inputs; every string has a fixed length, so each limb end hangs from its eyelet and the joints are solved analytically (torso = pendulum under the head string with the hips held by the back string, arms = two-bone IK under their eyelets, knees = sphere-sphere intersection, shins hang, feet stop on the floor) with a planned damped sway. Taut strings are straight, slack ones sag. Wood clacks, string creaks and plucks come from the same control plan.",
